{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_44","type":"agent_message","text":"The raw reinterpretation was too literal: the C source assigns `desc->sample_rate` into the union’s integer member, so it performs a floating-point-to-`u64` conversion first, including compiler-specific out-of-range behavior, and only then swaps those integer bytes. The remaining failures are all edge values from that conversion; I’m inspecting the built C instruction sequence and will reproduce that exact conversion rather than relying on Rust’s saturating `as` semantics."}}
