{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_48","type":"agent_message","text":"GCC emits a two-branch unsigned conversion using `cvttsd2si`: values below `2^63` use the signed conversion result directly, values at or above it subtract `2^63` and toggle the high bit, and invalid conversions return the x86 indefinite value. I’m encoding that exact behavior in a small helper, including NaN, infinities, and negative/out-of-range inputs, then applying the C byte swap."}}
